{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-resume-id-three-semantics",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 23 of the versioned inventory (contract L18/assertion 43): delegate_task's resume_id branch has THREE independent override semantics, none derivable from the others, plus its own tasks-follow-up check that never reaches the generic tasks validation. (1) provider is refused by TRUTHINESS — a non-empty provider is rejected with 'cannot switch provider when resuming a subagent', but provider:\"\" is falsy and ESCAPES the check entirely, letting the resume proceed. (2) max_iterations is refused by KEY PRESENCE, not value — even max_iterations:null is rejected with the resume-specific message, never L10's distinct '...not null' message (the resume branch wins the race). (3) model/effort are SILENTLY IGNORED during resume, never validated or rejected, resume proceeds normally as if they were absent. Also proves resume_id + tasks:[] / tasks:[\"   \"] produce the resume-specific 'resume_id requires a follow-up instruction' message, NOT the generic 'tasks must be a non-empty list'/'each task must be a non-empty string' messages a naive implementation would produce by validating tasks generically before checking resume semantics (this exact bug was found and fixed while building this manifest — see commit history). Finally proves the wire-level claim that a resumed child's second request carries exactly roles [system, user, assistant, user] — the resume is 'one-shot' at the call level, but the child's own history is NOT: it is the same persistent sub-session, continuing where it left off. Every rejected attempt costs zero upstream calls (validation-only); every accepted attempt costs exactly one real child round trip. Exactly the observable a unit test cannot prove: the candidate's own validateResumeOverrides/validateResumeTasks tests already verify the CANDIDATE's belief about these five oracle-authored messages; only the wire proves the oracle actually agrees.",
  "argv": [
    "chat",
    "SCEN:parent probes resume_id's three override semantics",
    "--json",
    "--provider",
    "ollama",
    "--model",
    "stub-coder:1b"
  ],
